{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum","id":1475855,"title":"(Storypath) Concerns about Momentum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-05T12:50:26-08:00","id":1475855,"title":"(Storypath) Concerns about Momentum?","content":"I've been skimming through the Trinity Continuum core rulebook, and I see some problems with the Momentum mechanic that I'm unsure how to fix. This is probably a Storypath system-wide thing, but I'm posting this here because TC is the only Storypath book I own so far and there's no &quot;general Storypath&quot; forum. I do plan to get more if these concerns are resolved, as Aberrant, Aeon, the They Came From books, and Dystopia Rising: Evolution all look very interesting.<br /> <br /> First of all, the rules as written don't allow Momentum to be spent without the permission of the entire group, and make it one pool for the entire group. If I run this, it's pretty much guaranteed that my players will get into arguments over when to spend it that wouldn't really take place if it was a per-character resource. In addition, it effectively makes it impossible to use Momentum in instances of conflict between PCs, especially during the vastly-more-common forms of non-combat conflict where a very relevant mechanic (skill tricks) would be completely shut down by PCs vetoing each other's momentum usage.<br /> <br /> Second, what prevents players from simply spamming low-risk rolls they know they're going to fail at to quickly replenish their Momentum pool? Right now, I don't see anything aside from GM fiat to prevent this, and quite frankly I'm confused as to why this mechanic incentivizes players to fail rolls because it results in absurd outcomes such as this.<br /> <br /> Third, how does Momentum work for major antagonist NPCs that have full character sheets, as suggested on page 138? How do they use Skill Tricks? Do they have their own Momentum pools or can they just use Skill Tricks without using Momentum?<br /> <br /> Are there any solutions to these problems, either official rules options in other books, or homebrew rules you would suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27327-endless-rain","name":"Endless Rain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T13:47:27-08:00","id":1475857,"title":"","content":"I have a house rule where Momentum is an individual shareable resource instead of a collective resource. That is, whoever generated the Momentum \u201cowns\u201d it, and has full say over how it can be used; but with his or her approval, anyone in the group can use it. I'm thinking of <i>maybe</i> pairing this with an option to the effect that you get a refund on your Momentum when you spend it on someone else and it doesn't work out: that is, if the roll fails and the guy who made the roll earns a point of Momentum in the process, you get your point of Momentum back; but only if <i>you're</i> not the guy who made the roll. The point is to minimize the risk of spending Momentum on someone else in the group and disincentivize hoarding. <br /> <br /> Second, I'd adapt a rule that exists in Hero Games: \u201ca Disadvantage that doesn't disadvantage you isn't worth any points\u201d. In Hero Games, it gives the GM permission to \u201czero out\u201d Disadvantages that are taken for the purpose of gaming the system. Here, the adaptation is to provide a guideline as to when \u201cStoryguide fiat\u201d is reasonable: if the failure of a particular skill roll doesn't actually cause any problems for anyone, then the Storyguide is well within his rights to veto the Momentum reward. That said, the real solution is to talk to the player who thinks that \u201cspamming for Momentum\u201d is a good idea and to try to get him or her into the mindset that Momentum is there to help promote the story, not the other way around. <br /> <br /> Officially, the Storyguide <i>is</i> free to activate Skill Tricks whenever he sees fit, just as he's free to add dice to rolls as he sees fit: in effect, he has an \u201cunlimited Momentum pool\u201d to \u201cspend\u201d however he likes. This is because his responsibility isn't playing a character; it's guiding the story. If you don't trust your Storyguide to do that, you've got bigger problems than whether or not a \u201cprimary antagonist\u201d has access to Momentum. That said, there's nothing preventing a Storyguide from imposing a limited Momentum Pool on himself, and only \u201cspending Momentum\u201d that he has \u201cearned\u201d. That said, such a pool ought to belong to the <i>Storyguide</i>, not to the <i>characters</i> \u2014 though if he wants to further subdivide his pool among various factions of antagonists (so that the failures of one such character doesn't empower another who's mutually antagonistic), he's free to do that, too. Just remember that any such restrictions like this are <i>entirely voluntary</i> and unenforceable: the Storyguide can make exceptions to this whenever he wishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T14:36:16-08:00","id":1475858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1475857#post1475857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a house rule where Momentum is an individual shareable resource instead of a collective resource. That is, whoever generated the Momentum \u201cowns\u201d it, and has full say over how it can be used; but with his or her approval, anyone in the group can use it. I'm thinking of <i>maybe</i> pairing this with an option to the effect that you get a refund on your Momentum when you spend it on someone else and it doesn't work out: that is, if the roll fails and the guy who made the roll earns a point of Momentum in the process, you get your point of Momentum back; but only if <i>you're</i> not the guy who made the roll. The point is to minimize the risk of spending Momentum on someone else in the group and disincentivize hoarding.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you suggest would be a good maximum for each individual's momentum pool? The corebook's default is 3 per character in the shared pool, so should it be 3? Or would you recommend raising it to compensate for the smaller pools per PC?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1475857#post1475857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I'd adapt a rule that exists in Hero Games: \u201ca Disadvantage that doesn't disadvantage you isn't worth any points\u201d. In Hero Games, it gives the GM permission to \u201czero out\u201d Disadvantages that are taken for the purpose of gaming the system. Here, the adaptation is to provide a guideline as to when \u201cStoryguide fiat\u201d is reasonable: if the failure of a particular skill roll doesn't actually cause any problems for anyone, then the Storyguide is well within his rights to veto the Momentum reward. That said, the real solution is to talk to the player who thinks that \u201cspamming for Momentum\u201d is a good idea and to try to get him or her into the mindset that Momentum is there to help promote the story, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vetoing consolation for failures that don't cause problems is reasonable, and I can do that. That being said, I would not be able to talk my group into changing their mindsets. We've been playing for a long time and I know that it just wouldn't work. Their mindset has usually been &quot;figure out what I want my character's goal to be in the story&quot; -&gt; &quot;find the fastest/easiest path using the rules to achieve that goal&quot; -&gt; &quot;use that plan to achieve the objective, even if it leads to actions that don't make any sense in-universe to get there&quot;, and I know them well enough that I don't see myself talking them out of it if I run a Storypath System game.<br /> <br /> This could easily lead to a path of: &quot;I want to break into this building to steal an item&quot; -&gt; &quot;I want to use a specific skill trick to get inside, and I'm all out of momentum&quot; -&gt; &quot;I will intentionally do something I'm bad at, which is irrelevant or detrimental to the story, with the minimum amount of negative consequences to earn Momentum, in the hopes that I fail and get Consolation&quot; -&gt; &quot;I will get a Momentum point and then spend it to get the thing I want&quot;.<br /> <br /> Usually, I've worked around around their playstyle by ensuring that the rules I play with don't incentivize characters to do things that it wouldn't make sense for them to want to do in-universe. I just can't figure out how to do this with Momentum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1475857#post1475857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially, the Storyguide <i>is</i> free to activate Skill Tricks whenever he sees fit, just as he's free to add dice to rolls as he sees fit: in effect, he has an \u201cunlimited Momentum pool\u201d to \u201cspend\u201d however he likes. This is because his responsibility isn't playing a character; it's guiding the story. If you don't trust your Storyguide to do that, you've got bigger problems than whether or not a \u201cprimary antagonist\u201d has access to Momentum. That said, there's nothing preventing a Storyguide from imposing a limited Momentum Pool on himself, and only \u201cspending Momentum\u201d that he has \u201cearned\u201d. That said, such a pool ought to belong to the <i>Storyguide</i>, not to the <i>characters</i> \u2014 though if he wants to further subdivide his pool among various factions of antagonists (so that the failures of one such character doesn't empower another who's mutually antagonistic), he's free to do that, too. Just remember that any such restrictions like this are <i>entirely voluntary</i> and unenforceable: the Storyguide can make exceptions to this whenever he wishes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is acceptable and more or less what I expected. I was simply unsure about the rules due to the very loose description of how to run full-character-sheet NPCs. I would most likely be the Storyguide if I ever ran this game, so not trusting myself is not an issue, though I would probably give such NPCs a limited, non-refilling momentum pool for the sake of balance and simplicity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27327-endless-rain","name":"Endless Rain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T17:04:11-08:00","id":1475865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Endless Rain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum#post1475855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, what prevents players from simply spamming low-risk rolls they know they're going to fail at to quickly replenish their Momentum pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>The \u201cWhen to Roll Dice\u201d rule on p. 69 is what stops this. \u201cWhen the stakes are high, and the consequences for failure are real, roll dice.\u201d Low-risk = no roll = no momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T04:58:12-08:00","id":1475980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Endless Rain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum#post1475855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, the rules as written don't allow Momentum to be spent without the permission of the entire group, and make it one pool for the entire group. If I run this, it's pretty much guaranteed that my players will get into arguments over when to spend it that wouldn't really take place if it was a per-character resource. In addition, it effectively makes it impossible to use Momentum in instances of conflict between PCs, especially during the vastly-more-common forms of non-combat conflict where a very relevant mechanic (skill tricks) would be completely shut down by PCs vetoing each other's momentum usage.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an incentive built into the system for spending Momentum, and that is that they get a group XP once per scene when they spend half the Momentum pool. My players generally encouraged each other to spend Momentum because they wanted to get that extra XP. Also, I never had a PC vs. PC roll, so the issue about being able to spend Momentum for those never came up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, what prevents players from simply spamming low-risk rolls they know they're going to fail at to quickly replenish their Momentum pool? Right now, I don't see anything aside from GM fiat to prevent this, and quite frankly I'm confused as to why this mechanic incentivizes players to fail rolls because it results in absurd outcomes such as this. </div> </div> </div>Bunyip already addressed this. If the roll is low-risk, don't have them roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third, how does Momentum work for major antagonist NPCs that have full character sheets, as suggested on page 138? How do they use Skill Tricks? Do they have their own Momentum pools or can they just use Skill Tricks without using Momentum? </div> </div> </div>Just let them use Skill Tricks when it is dramatically appropriate. Obviously don't apply a Skill Trick every roll, but go with the flow of the game.<br /> <br /> ETA: All that said, try actually running the game. It runs a bit different than other games, and your concerns may work out to be unfounded. I know they were not an issue in the 1.5 year long game I ran.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T15:50:56-08:00","id":1476003,"title":"","content":"There is another benefit of it being a group resource and that is, the pool is large enough to make a real difference when you use it. Plus, others can contribute to it to make it grow. If you did try to find some way to confine it (Like each player starts with 1 Momentum rather than it starting with 1 Momentum per each player) then the players would not be able to make it grow for when they need it the most.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T17:16:07-08:00","id":1476010,"title":"","content":"I find it's not a problem at my table, but that said, my players are not looking to fight one another. For the most part, Storypath rules work best when the intra-group conflict is kept minimal. You're working together to build a story, not get one over (or be better than) other players at the table.<br /> <br /> I find that the game also works far better with a shared pool over individual pools. A table of three players can build up to nine dice in the pool allowing for a Momentum use of 4-5 dice. Personal pools (without other changes) would limit the player to only 1-2 dice extra max which lacks the punch. The game also works well when <i><b>everyone's</b></i> failures contribute to <i><b>everyone's</b></i> successes, especially when you (like my table) approach it as a way of telling a story together.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, what other games does your table play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T06:25:53-08:00","id":1476092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476010#post1476010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it's not a problem at my table, but that said, my players are not looking to fight one another. For the most part, Storypath rules work best when the intra-group conflict is kept minimal. You're working together to build a story, not get one over (or be better than) other players at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been running Scion for over a year, which uses mostly the same Momentum system, and have to echo this sentiment. The players are generally happy to help each other succeed and being able to spend a ton of momentum for a big roll one player makes is something they're all happy about.<br /> <br /> Also with Momentum resetting every session they're keen to see someone spend it so they all get the experience for spending half the momentum pool in a single scene. Also to help with group cohesion we've started having everyone going over their short term aspirations at the start of the session, so the players can discuss how they'll help each other achieve at least one short term aspiration, and get another experience for it.<br /> <br /> Interparty conflict can lead to some neat story moments, but it helps if everyone is on board with that story and not trying to undercut each other. You might find the experience awards and how they reward everyone for doing group things can tempt your players to be aligned and not trying to stop the others from succeeding. Someone spending a ton of Momentum on one roll means everyone gets an xp, discussing their goals for the session can lead to mutually aligned aspirations so everyone gets an extra xp. The players can discuss how they want two characters to have a fight that session to get some things out in the open, and get rewarded for it.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd suggest trying it as a shared pool and using the carrot of bonus xp to get your players into it before going with individual pools.<br /> <br /> Scion presents individual momentum pools as an alternate rule on page 133 of Scion: Origin. In Scion the momentum pool isn't reset every session, so keep that in mind. In this alternate rule the book suggests a cap of 12 momentum for each player. Also if your players aren't failing rolls or engaging with Conditions very often they suggest an alternate rule where you hand out one momentum per scene or round of combat. If you did that, I'd def keep a lower cap than 12.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 03-09-2022, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:02:43-08:00","id":1476100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476092#post1476092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion presents individual momentum pools as an alternate rule on page 134 of Scion: Origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not finding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:36:13-08:00","id":1476107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476100#post1476100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not finding it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoops, was looking at the page of my pdf not the actual page number. Scion: Origin page 133, top right, Alternate Rules section, second option down. Begins with... &quot;<b>Individual Momentum Pools:</b> For groups who prefer a more individualized experience instead of a communal pool...&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll edit my post.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T22:38:57-08:00","id":1476149,"title":"","content":"I would also like to add that<br /> player vs player should only come into play as long as both parties agree to things ahead of time. By that, I mean that the only time players should bump heads is due to a long term growing rift. Even then, they should talk to each other and the GM ahead of time to discuss how it should end. In other words, should they resolve it or come to loggerheads at it or else to let it build up until it comes down to a battle (verbal or physical).<br /> Also, if it comes down to a battle between players, then I say do not allow a veto possible by the other party. For example, if you have Players A-E and Players A &amp; B have a dust up, then the only players that can veto something are Players C-E.<br /> Or else do not allow either side to use Momentum but you could do something like to allow them to spend an Inspiration to activate any Skill Tricks for the duration of the battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","user":"thedonnie","date":". 03-10-2022, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T00:08:48-08:00","id":1476151,"title":"","content":"I would heavily push two PCs that have some level of antagonism towards each other into a Rivalry Bond, and then let them spend Enhancements from the Bond pool instead of Momentum if they've actively come into conflict to power things like Skill Tricks. This preserves the Momentum pool for overcoming obstacles later, and the Bond pool running out as the two rivals finally decide to go at each other to resolve their current emotional state is entirely appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T00:25:41-08:00","id":1476152,"title":"","content":"Momentum is a Metaresource to bring the story forward and the base reason imho is SP as a colaborative game of experts. Thus I would not give them an individual one - or if fiven an individual one - they can't share until theyreunite the pool.<br /> <br /> Why not use the Rivalry Bond liek Heavy Arms said?<br /> But if your game's story devolves into hard infighting whre they want to use Skill Tricks on each other - I'd just divide the pool. But at my table the players would still be able to veto that momentum used - which keeps player agency alive - that another player fucks them over because they have a skill trick that can easily pummel that character.<br /> <br /> Or if you want to use Momentum PvP: They start with 0 - as they not acting as agroup - and can only build momentum in their PvP conflict - which would keep Momentum intact as medium to overcome setback. P1 hurt P2 - P2 get's momentum, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> A player spamming low risk rolls to farm Momentum? That sounds like gaming the game - and I would have a talk at your table to discourage that mindset. The resource of Momentum build on trust and collaboration and not to cheese the rules.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller i hardly use Momentum on the Nemesis side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T02:17:24-08:00","id":1476154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476152#post1476152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Momentum is a Metaresource to bring the story forward and the base reason imho is SP as a colaborative game of experts.</div> </div> </div> </div>While &quot;experts&quot; might not apply to every Storypath game, the system really is built around incentivizing the group to make characters that work together as a cohesive unit with each filling a niche for the group. This really can't be stressed enough. While interpersonal drama is certainly expected; it's meant to play out like it does in so much of the cited source material. Internal conflicts should push towards mutual respect and understanding so the group grows from it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T03:31:08-08:00","id":1476155,"title":"","content":"If players want their characters in conflict, consider letting them have individual Momentum pools, but each point they spend against the other character (activating Skill Tricks or extra dice) is paid to the other player for their use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T22:44:46-08:00","id":1476316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476010#post1476010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, what other games does your table play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly Pathfinder 1e, with a little experience with other D&amp;D editions. It works well for us for fantasy, but I'm considering breaking out into other genres. Right now I'm heavily considering a mixed-allegiance Aberrant campaign for our group's first supers campaign, with Aeon and Dystopia Rising as potential medium-term games for Sci-Fi and Post-Apocalyptic settings. Anything else Storypath is very low-priority to run at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476092#post1476092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion presents individual momentum pools as an alternate rule on page 133 of Scion: Origin. In Scion the momentum pool isn't reset every session, so keep that in mind. In this alternate rule the book suggests a cap of 12 momentum for each player. Also if your players aren't failing rolls or engaging with Conditions very often they suggest an alternate rule where you hand out one momentum per scene or round of combat. If you did that, I'd def keep a lower cap than 12.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense as a solution, and I would've missed it otherwise since Scion is a game I have very little interest in.<br /> <br /> But for the specifics of PvP skill tricks, I really like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476151#post1476151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would heavily push two PCs that have some level of antagonism towards each other into a Rivalry Bond, and then let them spend Enhancements from the Bond pool instead of Momentum if they've actively come into conflict to power things like Skill Tricks. This preserves the Momentum pool for overcoming obstacles later, and the Bond pool running out as the two rivals finally decide to go at each other to resolve their current emotional state is entirely appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This sounds absolutely perfect but... um... I can't find the Rivalry Bond in the Trinity Continuum core rulebook. It only has the Camaraderie, Friendship, and Love bonds. Is it included in one of the other books or is it something I have to homebrew?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27327-endless-rain","name":"Endless Rain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T00:24:20-08:00","id":1476317,"title":"","content":"Rivalry is in Scion:Origin, though the rules for Bonds based on negative emotions are in TC. So you'd have to &quot;homebrew&quot; it to do it out of TC core but the rules for how are right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T06:20:19-07:00","id":1476378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476317#post1476317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rivalry is in Scion:Origin, though the rules for Bonds based on negative emotions are in TC. So you'd have to &quot;homebrew&quot; it to do it out of TC core but the rules for how are right there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rivalry exists as a Fatebinding in Scion, which is a very different system than Bonds.<br /> <br /> There is a product on Drivetrhrurpg called &quot;The Storyguide's Guide to Guiding Stories: A Guide&quot; by Sean Creef, that has a homebrew Rivalry Bond in it. The book is full of lots of explanations of rules in TC, and commentary from someone who has been running games using the system for awhile, and lots of suggested house rules. I found it very helpful and worth the couple of bucks it cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T12:57:56-07:00","id":1476393,"title":"","content":"Rivalry is also an example Bond. Check out page 81.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T11:50:03-07:00","id":1476446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1475855-storypath-concerns-about-momentum?p=1476393#post1476393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rivalry is also an example Bond. Check out page 81.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair! I think I tend to forget about those descriptions in Scion because they're all mechanically the same (except for the situations where you can use the Enhancement), as opposed to TC where bonds are a little more chunky mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}